{
  "schema": "calcdb.question/1",
  "probe": "r-fix-cursor-dao/prop-user-appended-lifecycle",
  "bookRefs": [
    "R-DAO-1",
    "DAO-PROP"
  ],
  "description": "Repairs r-dao-1-err-1/prop-user-lifecycle: the held-after-Delete reads used pd, which was never appended (Value(\"\") gave 3385, Append 3386); the appended and deleted object was pdup, so held-Property behaviour across Delete and same-name recreation was untested. On TableDef T: a Property pa made by CreateProperty('P1', Text, 'init') and appended; Name, Type and Value of pa read; a duplicate P1 made by CreateProperty('P1', Text, 'dup') and appended, Errors; Type of pa put to Long, Errors; Value of pa put to 7, Null, Empty, each read back, Errors; Properties.Delete('P1'), Errors, then the HELD pa's Name and Value read with Errors after each; Delete('P1') again, Errors; a Property pnew made by CreateProperty('P1', Long, 9) and appended, Errors; the held pa's Value and pnew's Value read; the names of T's Properties enumerated. Then Close, a read-only reopen, and the reopened P1's Type and Value read. Asks what a held Property that WAS appended does across Delete and same-name recreation. The fixture copy is opened read-write.",
  "callerSurface": "native-idispatch/x64",
  "invokeLcid": 1033,
  "observationRecipe": [
    "clearErrorInfoBefore",
    "excepinfo",
    "deferredFill",
    "errorInfo"
  ],
  "pathBinding": "attempt-local-copy",
